Before the pr, we only need to extract point ranges from `cond`. Hence if `cond` has `origColNum`, we only need to consider whether the first `origColNum` columns of the index are constant. After the pr, we want to detect every constant column of the index (not only the first several columns). For example,
```
create table t2(a int, b int, c int, d int, index idx_a_b_c_d(a, b, c, d));
select * from t2 where ((a = 1 and b = 1 and d < 3) or (a = 1 and b = 1 and d > 6)) and c = 3 order by d;
```
In the case, when we deal with `c = 3`, `origColNum` is `1`. If we keep those lines, `currCols` and `currLengths` only include column `a` and we cannot detect `c = 3`.
